@codex review

Exact head `3644d2fb3ced860a2ad770bdb73daf1c065f3c7c`. Base: `claude/build-hone-saas-hOex7` @ `615ae92f1f1f9807f27cf4990c95b8e7e3b04afe`, behind 0. This head is a fast-forward of `2b6b28a2`, with no rebase or force-push. CI is green at this head (run 37228603610).

This head addresses the three findings from the review of `2b6b28a2`:

- **P1 (4178855061), isolate repository scripts from the runner process.** The runner no longer executes **any** code from the subject repository. `npm run verify:prepush`, the configurable pre-push command and the environment-sanitised child are all gone. CLAUDE.md delivery step 7 is replaced by trusted structural checks on the commit as data:
  - clean worktree, and HEAD/index/worktree identity;
  - `git diff --check`;
  - single child of the tip, generated-only scope, replace-not-overlay equality, runner authorship;
  - conflict markers and provenance.

  Commit and push use `--no-verify`, and the runner refuses to run from inside the subject clone. Repository-controlled verification stays in PR CI, where the runner's credentials are absent. A regression commits a hostile subject package (`verify:prepush`, `prepush`, `postinstall` and `test` all read `/proc/$PPID/environ` into a sentinel) and asserts that the sentinel never appears.
- **P2 (4178855066), preserve the new source head on metadata-only runs.** A metadata-only result is no longer discarded as NOOP. It is validated and published (`DRY_RUN` when publishing is off), so the processed source head becomes durable in repository state. A two-pass regression publishes, merges as a human would, and asserts that the next pass is a startup NOOP that never invokes OpenWiki.
- **P2 (4178855071), revalidate the base branch before pushing.** Immediately before the push, with the freshly minted publish token, the runner reads the exact remote SHA of `refs/heads/<base>`. If it differs from the pinned tip, nothing is published (`FAILED`, retried from the new tip). A deterministic regression advances production from inside the generator.

@codex review

Exact head `61c9496a93cfadca5f51b25023b331ecd34c434e`. Base: `claude/build-hone-saas-hOex7` @ `615ae92f1f1f9807f27cf4990c95b8e7e3b04afe`, behind 0. This head is a fast-forward of `3644d2fb`, with no rebase or force-push. CI is green at this head (run 37230548673).

This head addresses the two findings from the review of `3644d2fb`:

- **P2 (4179036263), recover when post-creation PR setup fails.** Once a pull request exists, the pass is `PUBLISHED` only if the PR head is exactly the verified commit **and** the exact-head `@codex review` request was posted. Any failure before that (`head-mismatch` or `review-request-failed`) runs `cleanUpCreatedPullRequest`. That closes the PR and deletes its branch, always attempting both, and records each step's state (`closed`/`close-failed`, `deleted`/`delete-failed`) with the PR number, branch and head. The pass then ends `FAILED`. If cleanup is incomplete, the next pass reports `SKIP` on the leftover branch. The GitHub client gains `closePullRequest` only; there is still no merge call. Six regressions cover:
  - a head mismatch;
  - a failed comment;
  - a failed branch delete, where the close is still attempted and the next pass is `SKIP`;
  - a failed close, where the delete is still attempted;
  - full success, with no cleanup;
  - no `PUBLISHED`, or any recorded outcome, until the review request has resolved.
- **P2 (4179036270), redact privacy terms before persisting generator output.** Generator output is no longer persisted at all. `runOpenWikiProcess` drains stdout/stderr into a byte count and a SHA-256 and keeps no text. Reports hold only `exitCode`, `timedOut`, `outputBytes` and `outputSha256`, and the CLI prints a fixed `cliSummary`. A regression emits a denylist term, a tenant slug, an email address, a phone number and two credential-shaped strings, then checks `last-run.json`, every `runs/*.json` and the CLI summary for none of them, on both a dry run and a failed run.
